First, we will create one or more unified kernel image(s) (UKI). This requires
adapting the configuration and preset files for mkinitcpio and customizing the
kernel command line. This script should take care of most of the work but each
config file will be opened with a text editor ($EDITOR) so you can make custom
adjustments.
One thing to note is that we will be using a systemd based initramfs. ArchLinux
by default uses busybox but using systemd gives us access to a couple of handy
extensions during the boot process.